/F2 13.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 760 Tm (Government Policies) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 737 Tm (A price ceiling is a legal maximum on the price at which a good can be sold. Rent control is) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 721.5 Tm (a common example of a price ceiling. A binding price ceiling causes a shortage.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 701.0 Tm (A price floor is a legal minimum on the price at which a good can be sold. The minimum wage) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 685.5 Tm (is an example of a price floor. A binding price floor causes a surplus.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 665.0 Tm (A tax on a good places a wedge between the price buyers pay and the price sellers receive.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 649.5 Tm (Tax incidence is the manner in which the burden of a tax is shared among participants in a) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 634.0 Tm (market.) Tj
/F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 280 30 Tm (Page 3 of 3) Tj
